1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,819
Meet Luma Goods, an independent seller running a Shopify website.

2
00:00:03,819 --> 00:00:07,345
They need to know whether a new release helps customers buy.

3
00:00:07,345 --> 00:00:08,814
ImpactGuard starts green.

4
00:00:08,814 --> 00:00:17,452
This local demo uses synthetic traffic and projects impact for one hundred and twenty checkout starts per day, at an eighty two dollar order value.

5
00:00:18,452 --> 00:00:21,775
A payment redirect change now hurts checkout completion.

6
00:00:21,775 --> 00:00:22,962
The issue turns red.

7
00:00:22,962 --> 00:00:30,082
ImpactGuard estimates six hundred and ninety dollars a day in revenue exposure for this seller, if the pattern persists.

8
00:00:30,082 --> 00:00:34,829
This is a calculated scenario projection, not a claim about actual lost revenue.

9
00:00:35,829 --> 00:00:39,901
The investigation separates Safari and PayPal from other customers.

10
00:00:39,901 --> 00:00:44,946
Their completion rate drops from about seventy two percent to thirty eight percent.

11
00:00:44,946 --> 00:00:47,256
Other segments stay close to baseline.

12
00:00:47,256 --> 00:00:52,300
The engine shows sample counts, statistical evidence, and the exact dollar formula.

13
00:00:53,300 --> 00:00:56,291
The suspect commit changed PayPal token handling.

14
00:00:56,291 --> 00:01:00,808
ImpactGuard ranks it using timing, service files, and relevant diff terms.

15
00:01:00,808 --> 00:01:03,859
Developers can inspect the changed lines directly.

16
00:01:03,859 --> 00:01:07,338
The score identifies a plausible investigation candidate.

17
00:01:07,338 --> 00:01:10,573
It does not prove that the commit caused the problem.

18
00:01:11,573 --> 00:01:14,199
We simulate rolling back the faulty behavior.

19
00:01:14,199 --> 00:01:21,143
ImpactGuard generates six thousand fresh sessions and measures recovered checkout completion, near seventy two percent.

20
00:01:21,143 --> 00:01:23,477
The state turns green after measurement.

21
00:01:23,477 --> 00:01:26,803
No production rollback or external account action occurs.

22
00:01:27,803 --> 00:01:30,439
The next change combines two coupon discounts.

23
00:01:30,439 --> 00:01:33,190
Orders can look healthy while profit disappears.

24
00:01:33,190 --> 00:01:41,156
ImpactGuard finds negative contribution margin and projects about twelve hundred and thirty five dollars a week of exposure for Luma Goods.

25
00:01:41,156 --> 00:01:44,021
The investigation points to the discount combiner.

26
00:01:45,021 --> 00:01:47,732
Delivery changes can also affect the seller.

27
00:01:47,732 --> 00:01:53,522
Mature synthetic customer cohorts show much lower repeat purchase rates after late deliveries.

28
00:01:53,522 --> 00:01:58,265
The annual number is an explicit scenario projection scaled to seller volume.

29
00:01:58,265 --> 00:02:03,255
Customer mix remains a possible explanation, so the finding stays an association.

30
00:02:04,255 --> 00:02:06,407
The same approach extends to banking.

31
00:02:06,407 --> 00:02:10,303
A callback mapper marks failed and pending transfers as successful.

32
00:02:10,303 --> 00:02:15,770
ImpactGuard compares two thousand bank outcomes with application statuses and ledger postings.

33
00:02:15,770 --> 00:02:21,063
It finds two hundred mismatches and about forty seven thousand dollars in unbacked credits.

34
00:02:22,063 --> 00:02:23,830
The diff exposes the mistake.

35
00:02:23,830 --> 00:02:30,350
Explicit checks for settled, failed, and pending statuses were replaced by a fallback that reports success.

36
00:02:30,350 --> 00:02:33,640
Application success is not evidence that cash arrived.

37
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:40,830
Banking amounts use integer cents, and the reconciliation check evaluates ledger postings against settlement evidence.

38
00:02:41,830 --> 00:02:47,188
Remediation records two hundred corrective reversals and retains the original credits.

39
00:02:47,188 --> 00:02:51,051
The system verifies zero remaining mismatches and turns green.

40
00:02:51,051 --> 00:02:56,285
The project runs locally, with no Shopify, GitHub, bank, or cloud account connected.

41
00:02:56,285 --> 00:03:01,083
A real customer pilot would connect verified releases and business telemetry.
